{
  "slug": "harness-evolver",
  "name": "Harness Evolver",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Autonomous LLM agent optimization using LangSmith. Spawns 5 parallel proposers in git worktrees, evaluates candidates via LangSmith experiments, and merges winners automatically. Includes evaluator agent (LLM-as-judge via langsmith-cli), critic, architect, and testgen agents. No external API keys needed beyond LangSmith.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **6 agents** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `certify` (Use when the user wants to verify that the evolved agent's score is stable and reliable), `deploy` (Use when the user is done evolving and wants to finalize, clean up, tag the result, or push…), `evolve` (Use when the user wants to run the optimization loop, improve agent performance, evolve the agent, or iterate…), `health` (Use when the user wants to check dataset quality, diagnose eval issues, or before running evolve), `setup` (Use when the user wants to set up the evolver in their project, optimize an LLM agent, improve…), `status` (Use when the user asks about evolution progress, current scores, best version, how many iterations ran, or whether…)\n- **Agents** (6): `harness-architect` (Use this agent when the evolution loop stagnates or regresses), `harness-consolidator` (Background agent for cross-iteration memory consolidation), `harness-critic` (Use this agent when scores converge suspiciously fast, evaluator quality is questionable, or the agent reaches high scores…), `harness-evaluator` (Use this agent to evaluate experiment outputs using LLM-as-judge), `harness-proposer` (Self-organizing agent optimizer), `harness-testgen` (Use this agent to generate test inputs for the evaluation dataset)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install harness-evolver@claude-community` from `raphaelchristi/harness-evolver`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "agent": 6,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Raphael Valdetaro"
  },
